  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: Nigeria-Dutch horticulture collaboration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The partnership has the objective to speed up the implementation of protected cultivation and soilless farming techniques among Nigerian farmers. Through this program the Nigerian business climate will improve on: &#x2022;	Opportunities for farmers through improved training programs in protected cultivation leading into business start-ups, improvements, and scale-ups. &#x2022;	Increase employment options in the agricultural sector, job creation for Nigerians, including youth and women. &#x2022;	Increased production of safe vegetables by adaptation of new innovative technologies and monitoring methodologies for the Nigerian setting. &#x2022;	Establishment of a demonstration greenhouse, upgrading of the existing training and demonstration facilities and connection to the international horticulture environment. &#x2022;	Increased collaboration among Dutch and Nigerian companies, non-gournmental organizations (NGO&#x2019;s) and knowledge institutes. The ultimate aim is to establish a sustainable business cooperation from which, in the long term, &#x2022;	The Nigerian farmer community will benefit from the improved knowledge, enhanced productivity and increased sales levels of agricultural produce; &#x2022;	The Dutch industry partners will benefit from increased sales levels of Dutch horticulture technique, inputs and knowledge; and &#x2022;	The Nigerian business partners will benefit due to expansion of horticulture activities in sales, training and business development.</narrative>
  </description>
